agent/data/
*.whatsapp.txt
WhatsApp Chat*

# Secrets
.env
*.env

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Node (only pulled in locally for browser-based verification — never deployed)
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json

# NOTE: coverage.json is deliberately NOT ignored. It used to be listed here as
# a "Trends intermediate ... not browser-facing", but that was wrong: index.html
# fetches coverage.json directly to fill each outlet card's "show all headlines"
# expander (see the loadCoverage() block). Ignoring it made the `git add
# coverage.json` in fetch-headlines.yml fail silently — git refuses to add an
# ignored path, and the `2>/dev/null || true` there swallowed the error — so the
# file was never committed, never deployed, and the expander fetched a 404 and
# fell back to an empty list on every open. Keep it tracked.
